    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) standing as our most efficient option. Batting leadoff against the vulnerable 4.71 xERA of Chandler, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** provides the perfect intersection of high-frequency stolen base potential and a favorable platoon advantage (+14%). Close behind him, **Trea Turner** (75.36) and **Yordan Alvarez** (70.49) serve as the engines of our offense; while **Yordan Alvarez** faces a tougher arm in Peralta, his elite .443 xwOBA effectively renders the pitcher's quality secondary. We are also capitalizing on **Colt Keith** (68.51) and **Junior Caminero** (67.39), both of whom benefit significantly from positive lineup positioning and soft matchups, allowing us to stack high-upside bats in the heart of the order.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (40.50), who ultimately landed on the bench. Despite his power potential, the combination of a difficult matchup against Cease (3.02 xERA) and the superior efficiency ratings of **Kazuma Okamoto** (58.49) and **Christian Yelich** (53.75) pushed him out of the starting nine. We remain cautious with **Carson Benge** (46.11); while he earns a start, his low score is a direct consequence of facing Schlittler, an elite pitcher with a 2.88 xERA. We are monitoring **Dillon Dingler** (49.35) and **Gary Sanchez** (41.84) closely, as their efficiency scores are hampered by sub-optimal matchups that hover near our benching threshold. With **Casey Schmitt**, **Josh Smith**, and **Jacob Gonzalez** unavailable due to injury or rest, our lineup depth is being tested, making it imperative that our high-scoring anchors like **Lars Nootbaar** (65.03) provide the necessary production to offset the marginal plays at the bottom of the order.",
